+	// -----------------------------------------------------------------------
+	// Per-character static placement scale
+	// -----------------------------------------------------------------------
+	// The curve-flattening tolerance is expressed in shape-DEFINITION twips, so
+	// it is blind to placement scale: a small curve composed at 8x is flattened
+	// as coarsely as one composed at 1x and carries eight times the error onto
+	// the screen (`wave1-gfx-curvejoint.md` §3.3 measures the corpus-wide
+	// residual — 6 tests above 0.10 px, all of them scale-amplified). This
+	// pre-pass walks the tag stream once, before recompilation, and records for
+	// each character the largest static scale it is ever composed at —
+	// propagated through DefineSprite nesting, since a sprite's own placement
+	// scales everything inside it. interpretShape divides the tolerance by it.
+	//
+	// Scales are floored at 1.0, so a character that is never scaled up is
+	// flattened exactly as before and the corpus-wide diff is confined to the
+	// handful of tests that do scale one up. AS-driven _xscale/scaleX is
+	// invisible to a static pass; that degrades to today's behaviour, and the
+	// failure direction is a coarser curve, never a wrong one.
